          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Generally, given some kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            equipped with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+points"} fixed points
            of the action may form a suitable sub-space: the
            = succeed "." do
              %em fixed point space
          %h3#for_topological_spaces
            For topological
            = succeed "-spaces" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            Specifically, given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-space"} topological G-space
            %em fixed point space
            is the set of the set-theoretic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+points"} fixed points
            of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
          %p
            For more see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-space"} topological G-space
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "topological+G-space#ChangeOfGroupsAndFixedLoci"} Change of groups and fixed loci
          %h3#in_equivariant_homotopy_theory In equivariant homotopy theory
          %p
            The statement of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elmendorf%27s+theorem"} Elmendorf's theorem
            is essentially that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-space"}
              topological
              = succeed "-spaces" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is equivalently encoded in their systems of
            = succeed "-fixed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            varies over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspace"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %h3#in_equivariant_stable_homotopy_theory In equivariant stable homotopy theory
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} equivariant stable homotopy theory
            the concept of fixed point spaces branches into various closely related, but different concepts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+spectra"}> fixed point spectra
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+fixed+point+spectra"} geometric fixed point spectra
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord
                  categorical fixed point spectra
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/categorical+fixed+point+spectra"} ?
          %h3#in_equivariant_differential_topology In equivariant differential topology
          %p
            In
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+differential+topology"} equivariant differential topology
          #ExistenceOfGInvariantTubularNeighbourhoods.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (existence of
                = succeed "-invariant" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tubular+neighbourhoods"} tubular neighbourhoods
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \;\colon\; G \times X \to X
              a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+action"} proper
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphisms"} diffeomorphisms
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
